#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""vpn-bot-protocol-install — install ONE protocol on this host, strictly by the manifest
compiled into this file (docs/protocol-install.md).

The mirror of deploy/helpers/vpn-bot-protocol-uninstall: what this helper installs for a
protocol (OWNED: its units, unit files, paths, packages, users, the <PROTO>_ENABLED flag)
is exactly what the uninstall removes, and the uninstall marker it takes away last is the
one the uninstall writes last (tests/test_protocol_install_helper.py pins the symmetry
against the uninstall's own `manifest <proto>`). What a protocol needs but does not own —
nginx and the decoy site, the certificate's registry, the user `nobody` — is SHARED: put in
place when it is missing, never removed by an uninstall (its deny-list says the same).

  vpn-bot-protocol-install manifest <proto> [--json]      the resolved manifest (review)
  vpn-bot-protocol-install status [--json]                which protocols are on this host
  vpn-bot-protocol-install plan <proto> [--domain D] [--json]
                                                          read-only: every change, a sha256
  vpn-bot-protocol-install apply <proto> --expect-plan SHA [--domain D] [--json]
                                                          backup, the steps, a journal; any
                                                          failure rolls the steps back
  vpn-bot-protocol-install verify <proto> [--domain D] [--json]
                                                          read-only: the protocol works
  vpn-bot-protocol-install rollback <proto> [--json]      undo the last apply (its journal)
  vpn-bot-protocol-install commit <proto> [--json]        the last apply is final (verified)

  <proto>: xray

XRAY (with the nginx self-steal). The layout of the production host: the binary of an
official GitHub release of a PINNED version (/usr/local/bin/xray, the geo files in
/usr/local/share/xray) — the zip's sha256 is pinned here AND must be the SHA2-256 line of
the release's own .dgst; the upstream units xray.service / xray@.service with the
single-config drop-ins (deploy/xray/); /usr/local/etc/xray/config.json nobody:vpn-bot 0640
(nobody:nogroup without the vpn-bot group: the root model), generated from
deploy/xray/config.skeleton.json — a fresh x25519 pair (`xray x25519`), one shortId,
REALITY target 127.0.0.1:8443, serverNames = the domain, the XHTTP fallback inbound on
127.0.0.1:8001, the api inbound on 127.0.0.1:10085 — serialized exactly as the bot writes
it, so the bot's reconcile, the deploy's drift check (deploy/backend-config-sync.py) and
the bot's own rewrite leave it byte for byte as it is; /var/log/xray. Then the XRAY_* of
.env (one line per key changed or appended, owner and mode kept, .env in the backup first).
nginx: the package (policy-rc.d holds it from starting with its default site on :80; the
default site of a package installed HERE is disabled), the decoy site from
deploy/site/default and deploy/nginx/selfsteal.conf (127.0.0.1:8443, TLS 1.3, h2, the
certificate of the registry, /etc/vpn-bot/tls) — nginx becomes a reader of
`vpn-bot-cert` (docs/certificate.md) by existing, and `vpn-bot-cert deploy` lays the pair
out to it. A host that already runs its own self-steal on 127.0.0.1:8443 keeps it.

APPLY, in this order — each step writes its journal entry BEFORE it acts, so a failure (or
a kill) half way is undone too; a failure rolls every step back in reverse:
  preflight   the plan recomputed: its sha256 must be the one confirmed (else exit 3)
  backup      every existing path a step may change, .env included, in
              /var/backups/vpn-bot/install/<proto>-<UTC ts>.tar.gz (root 0600), verified
  nginx_pkg   apt-get install nginx (when not installed), its default site off
  nginx_start nginx enabled and active (with no vhost of ours yet: it reads no certificate)
  cert        vpn-bot-cert deploy — the registry's pair laid out to nginx
  nginx_site  the decoy site and selfsteal.conf, nginx -t, reload
  xray_bin    download, sha256 against the pin and the .dgst, the binary and geo files
  xray_units  the unit files and drop-ins, daemon-reload
  xray_logs   /var/log/xray and its two files (`xray run -test` opens them)
  xray_config config.json, checked with `xray run -test` BEFORE it is put in place
  env         the XRAY_* of .env
  xray_start  enable --now xray, active
  marker      /etc/vpn-bot/uninstalled/<proto> removed (a reinstall) — the LAST step

What exists is never replaced (an installed xray, config.json with its clients, an
operator's nginx): the plan says `keep`, the step leaves it. A repeated apply on an
installed protocol is "nothing to do".

EXIT CODES: 0 ok · 2 usage · 3 refused (a blocking finding, a plan that changed, another
install or uninstall runs, committed) · 4 verify failed · 5 cannot (a tool, a file, a
download) · 6 a step failed and the rollback succeeded · 7 a step failed and the rollback
did not fully succeed.

Stdlib only, every command an argv list (never a shell). Run as root from another mount
namespace (the non-root bot's ProtectSystem=strict, kept by sudo) it re-executes itself in
PID 1's first (nsenter). TEST SEAM (never in production; sudo and systemd-run give a clean
environment): VPN_BOT_PROTOCOL_INSTALL_SELFTEST=1 needs VPN_BOT_PROTOCOL_INSTALL_ROOT
(every host path under it) and VPN_BOT_PROTOCOL_INSTALL_REPO (the checkout), resolves every
command inside VPN_BOT_PROTOCOL_INSTALL_SELFTEST_BIN, reads release assets from
VPN_BOT_PROTOCOL_INSTALL_SELFTEST_RELEASES instead of the network, keeps owners in a
sidecar file instead of chown, and _SELFTEST_FAIL=<step> fails right after that step did
its work — deploy.sh runs the test suite as root on the production host.
"""
